# SelectIQ — Code Owners
#
# Paths listed here require review from their owner before a pull request can
# be merged. Ownership is defined in CLAUDE.md ("Security Rules") and covers
# the files where a mistake is expensive: the data model, the exam gate, the
# auth server keys, and the guardrail documents themselves.
#
# NOTE: This file only takes effect once branch protection on `main` has
# "Require review from Code Owners" enabled. Without that, it is documentation.
#
# Syntax: <path pattern>  <owner>
# Later matches win, so the most specific rule must come last.

# --- Database schema and migrations -------------------------------
# Every one of the 142 tables lands here. A bad migration is hard to undo.
/prisma/                      @manuVrtti

# --- Exam link enforcement (Layer 2) ------------------------------
# Gates every /exam/* route. A regression here lets candidates sit exams
# outside the locked-down Electron browser.
/src/proxy.ts                 @manuVrtti

# --- Server-side auth ---------------------------------------------
# Reads FIREBASE_ADMIN_PRIVATE_KEY. Must never be imported client-side.
/src/lib/firebase-admin.ts    @manuVrtti

# --- Environment files --------------------------------------------
# .env and .env.local are git-ignored, so in practice this guards
# .env.example — the one env file that ships to GitHub.
.env*                         @manuVrtti

# --- Guardrail documents ------------------------------------------
# These steer every AI-assisted change in the repo.
/CLAUDE.md                    @manuVrtti
/.cursorrules                 @manuVrtti
